### Lab: Scaling Deployments with Kubectl

	kubectl scale deploy nginx-deployment --replicas=3 
	
This is only a temporary change and the yaml file remains
unchanged so the kubectl apply will restore the number of
replicas to the value indicated in the deploymnt yaml file.

### Lab: Troubleshooting Failed Rollouts

Check the rollout status

	kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx-deployment
	
Also look at the status of the pods

	kubectl get pod
	
Temporary solution is to issue the *rollout undo* command, but
that will only poersist until the next *apply* issued and the failure
will re-occur.

	kubectl rollout undo deployment nginx-deployment
	
Permanent fix is to fix/modify the yaml file so the next *apply*
does nopt fail.


